    "narrative": "For LawDog on May 6, 2026, **Cal Raleigh** stands as our premier start with a score of 75.80. He benefits from a prime matchup against Martin P\u00e9rez, whose 4.73 xERA provides the most favorable pitcher environment of the day. By hitting second, **Cal Raleigh** maximizes his run-production ceiling, bolstered by a significant SP skill adjustment. While **Tyler Freeman** (58.65) falls just short of the elite threshold, he remains a high-floor play due to the synergy between his 92% stolen base success rate against the pitcher's slow delivery and a park factor boost of +14%. His ability to manufacture steals remains critical given our league's scarcity-driven prioritization of speed.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the profiles of our outfielders, as **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Taylor Ward**, and **Gavin Sheets** all hovered near the 50-point mark. **Gavin Sheets** (53.78) earns the start over his peers primarily due to the soft matchup against Houser, though his score is tempered slightly by a poor BvP history. Conversely, **Lawrence Butler** (50.64) is an intriguing start; despite facing an elite arm in Wheeler, the combination of favorable wind conditions and a strong platoon edge makes him a viable option. We are closely monitoring the status of **Daulton Varsho**, who remains benched due to his absence from today's official lineup; had he been confirmed, his stolen base upside against a slower delivery would have necessitated a reconsideration of our middle infield slots currently held by **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Jeremiah Jackson**. Note the inherent risk with **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, both of whom face high-level pitching in Paul Skenes and Cole Ragans, respectively; while these matchups suppress their raw efficiency, their lineup placement keeps them squarely in the lineup to ensure we don't bleed category production.",
